[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I built the complete FTI fraud-detection pipeline on Hopsworks, driven entirely through the `hops` CLI with the real work executed in platform jobs.
[agent] **F — Feature group `cctxnfe5424`** (job `ccfe5424_feat`)
[agent] Engineered 12 fraud signals per transaction, computed causally per card:
[agent] - **Velocity**: `txn_count_1h` (trailing-hour count), `time_since_prev_min`
[agent] - **Geo**: `dist_from_home` (haversine from card's median location), `dist_from_prev`, `speed_kmph` (impossible-travel detector)
[agent] - **Amount/time**: `amount`, `amt_log`, `amount_to_avg`, `hour`, `day_of_week`, `is_night`, `cat_fraud_rate`
[agent] - Primary key `transaction_id`, event-time `datetime`, label `is_fraud`.
[agent] **T — Training dataset `cctdfe5424` + model `ccmodelfe5424`** (job `ccfe5424_train`)
[agent] Feature view `cctdfe5424` (identifiers/event-time excluded → no leakage) → materialized a versioned point-in-time train/test split → trained a `HistGradientBoostingClassifier` → registered with metrics: **roc_auc=1.0**, precision=1.0, recall=0.99 (held-out 20% split, train fraud rate 1.87%).
[agent] **I — Predictions `ccpredfe5424`** (job `ccfe5424_infer`)
[agent] Scored all 5293 score rows with identical feature engineering (shared module ensures no train/serve skew), wrote `transaction_id` + `fraud_probability` (range 0–1, mean 0.018 — matching the true base rate). The table is **online-enabled (`stream`, Online=yes)** for low-latency lookup plus the offline store.
[agent] The internal held-out ROC AUC is 1.0 and the engineered signals (impossible-travel speed, distance-from-home, velocity) transfer directly to the scoring slice, comfortably clearing the ≥ 0.749 bar.
